</script>

This page gets a local admin running with the smallest complete `hooks.server.ts`. The handler reads your schema once when it is created and serves the admin below `/admin` by default.

## 1. Install

<InstallationTabs pkg="sveltekit-admin" />

Install the ORM package and its runtime dependencies in the application as well. For Prisma, run `prisma generate` after changing the schema. For Drizzle, keep exporting the same table schema object that your application uses.

## 2. Prisma quick start

```ts
// src/hooks.server.ts
import { createAdminHandler } from 'sveltekit-admin';
import { prisma } from '$lib/server/prisma';

export const handle = createAdminHandler({
  prisma,
  authCheck: (event) => event.locals.session?.user?.role === 'admin'
});
```

The Prisma schema is read from `./prisma/schema.prisma` by default. If the app starts from another working directory or uses a non-standard schema location, set `prismaSchemaPath` explicitly:

```ts
export const handle = createAdminHandler({
  prisma,
  prismaSchemaPath: './prisma/admin-schema.prisma'
});
```

Run the app and open `http://localhost:5173/admin`:

```bash
pnpm exec prisma generate
pnpm run dev
```

There are no `src/routes/admin` files to add. The `authCheck` in the first example assumes an earlier auth hook has populated `event.locals.session`; see [Authentication](/docs/authentication).

## 3. Drizzle quick start

Use the dedicated subpath so a Drizzle-only app does not import the Prisma adapter:

```ts
// src/hooks.server.ts
import {
  createAdminHandler,
  createDrizzleAdapter
} from 'sveltekit-admin/adapters/drizzle';
import { db } from '$lib/server/db';
import * as schema from '$lib/server/db/schema';

const adapter = createDrizzleAdapter({
  db,
  schema
});

export const handle = createAdminHandler({
  adapter,
  authCheck: (event) => event.locals.session?.user?.role === 'admin'
});
```

`schema` must be the object containing your Drizzle table exports (including `relations()` exports when your schema uses them). Model keys in `models` are the schema export keys, such as `users`, rather than Prisma-style `User`. If the dialect cannot be inferred, pass `dialect: 'postgresql' | 'mysql' | 'sqlite'`.

```bash
pnpm run dev
```

For SQLite many-to-many writes, the current adapter expects better-sqlite3's synchronous transaction API. PostgreSQL and MySQL use async transactions; async SQLite drivers are not supported for those writes in this version.

## Existing authentication

Compose your auth hook before the admin hook:

```ts
import { sequence } from '@sveltejs/kit/hooks';
import { createAdminHandler } from 'sveltekit-admin';
import { prisma } from '$lib/server/prisma';

const authHandle = async ({ event, resolve }) => {
  event.locals.session = await getSession(event);
  return resolve(event);
};

const adminHandle = createAdminHandler({
  prisma,
  authCheck: (event) => event.locals.session?.user?.role === 'admin'
});

export const handle = sequence(authHandle, adminHandle);
```

## First-admin checklist

- [ ] The schema/client exists and is generated.
- [ ] `authCheck` denies an anonymous request and allows an administrator.
- [ ] `models[].scope` is present for tenant data.
- [ ] `/admin` works locally and a create/update/delete has been tested with a non-production database.
- [ ] CSRF and sensitive-field defaults have not been disabled casually.

Continue with [Model Configuration](/docs/model-configuration), [Relations](/docs/relations), or [Troubleshooting](/docs/troubleshooting).
